# Bulk solver artifacts - regenerated and hash-matched, never committed
evidence/drat/
*.drat
evidence/**/*.cnf
evidence/*.cnf

# A wave's per-cube proofs, stored compressed. `*.drat` above does not match
# `cube00000.drat.gz`, whose suffix is `.gz`, so it is named here explicitly.
# What is committed for a wave is the manifest, the per-cube verdicts and the
# per-cube transcripts; the proofs are bulk and the cube instances they were
# checked against regenerate from the manifest.
*.drat.gz
evidence/waves/**/proofs/

# The DIMACS writer streams the body to a sibling temp file and unlinks it in a
# finally block. A killed run skips that, and the leftover is named
# `<instance>.cnf.body.tmp`, which the `*.cnf` patterns above do not match.
*.body.tmp

# Local scratch - ARTEFACTS ONLY.
#
# This was a bare `scratch/` until 2026-08-24, which meant the ENTIRE campaign
# pipeline - orchestrator, wave driver, pruner, checker, watchdog, the console
# and durability fixes and all their tests - lived in a gitignored directory
# with no backup anywhere. `git status` reported the clone clean and
# `git ls-remote` confirmed HEAD was on origin, so an idle-clone cleanup
# deleted it: 99.1 GB of results and six days of pipeline source, gone, with
# both safety checks reporting green. A CLEAN TREE IS NOT AN EMPTY DIRECTORY.
#
# The SOURCE is tracked from here on. Only the multi-gigabyte artefacts and
# the machine-local run state are ignored.
# A wave directory is gigabytes of verdicts and proofs, so its CONTENTS are
# ignored - but not the small files that are pure evidence.
#
# manifest.json is 560 bytes and carries the encoder, the split vars, the cube
# construction and the sha256 of base.cnf and cubes.txt. sample.json is 10 KB
# and carries the seed and method the 1,600-cube proof sample was drawn with.
# Those hashes are the entire reason a regenerated base.cnf can be trusted to
# be the same input the verdicts were computed against, and the seed is the
# only thing that makes the sample reproducible.
#
# On 2026-08-24 they existed in exactly one place on one disk. They were inside
# the directory the deletion above took, and survived only because someone had
# pasted them into a note. Evidence that small does not belong behind an ignore
# rule written for gigabytes.
#
# Note the trailing `*`: git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is
# excluded, so this ignores the directory's CONTENTS rather than the directory
# itself, which is what lets the negations below apply at all.
scratch/wave*/*
!scratch/wave*/manifest.json
!scratch/wave*/sample.json
scratch/nk2snap/
scratch/*.log
scratch/*.pid
scratch/*.pid.error
scratch/__pycache__/
scratch/*.jsonl

# The watchdog's desktop notice. It is machine-local run state in the same way
# the logs and pid files above are - the watchdog writes it and opens it in
# Notepad to get the operator's attention, and on 2026-08-28 it carried the
# GOOD news ("this is the good one"). DONE.json is the durable record of the
# same event and IS committed; this is the transient copy addressed to a human.
scratch/CAMPAIGN_ATTENTION.txt

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
